{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC5 first live run: `passed=false`, but the picture improved and the remaining failures are informative.\n\nBaseline on origin/main had 6 distinct failing cases. After AC1–AC4 it is 3, and all three are `FP-loc-*`: FP-loc-ceiling-single-sourced-mirror (2/3), FP-loc-numeric-budget-not-a-file-size (2/3), FP-loc-anti-fragmentation-floor (1/3). coverage 1.0, elapsed 1643s. Every fixture the ACs name now passes.\n\nI assumed the loc family was the reviewer over-generalizing the loc-ceiling antipattern to any `<= N` bound, and that assumption was wrong. Capturing the actual Pass-1 findings for those three cases showed the reviewer is correct in each, and firing under different guards than loc-ceiling-pinning:\n\n- FP-loc-anti-fragmentation-floor references `line_counts`, which is undefined in test_get_rotation.py. The reviewer searched the file, reported `(no matches)`, and noted the assertion would raise NameError. That is AC2's defect class exactly, in a case AC2 does not name.\n- FP-loc-numeric-budget-not-a-file-size asserts only `len(base) + len(out) <= 500`, which passes as `0 <= 500` on an empty prefetch. That is AC3's defect class exactly, in a case AC3 does not name.\n\nSo the ticket's Cause B — defective fixtures — is real in 6 cases, not the 4 the ACs enumerate. The two extras are the same two defect classes already named, so this is an enumeration gap in the ACs rather than new work, and AC5 cannot report passed=true while they stand. Fixed both in place; no case added or removed, header untouched.\n\nTwo further corrections the reviewer earned, worth recording because both were my errors, not its:\n\n1. My AC2 fix invented an API. I wrote `from rebar.module_size_support import ...` and called `gate_file_loc(p)` per path. The reviewer checked the real helper and reported that `gate_file_loc()` is zero-arg and already returns the whole `{path: loc}` mapping, that the module lives at `tests/module_size_support.py` and is imported as `from module_size_support import ...`, and that no `src/rebar/module_size_support.py` exists. I verified all three against the tree — it was right on every point. The fixture now uses `gate_file_loc()` zero-arg with the existing import block.\n2. An intermediate version asserted `all(count <= limit for ...)`, and the reviewer flagged that it discards which module violated, citing the sibling `test_no_src_module_over_the_hard_cap` that reports the offending set. Also correct; the fixture now builds an `over` dict and asserts it is empty with the violators in the message.\n\nTargeted re-check of just those three cases against the live model: 0 findings each. Full 3-epoch eval re-running now for AC5."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793819948778067713,"uuid":"2ae10ba3-96f0-4b37-8bf8-aae21f62e6c2"}